 ### Source limitations
 
-The original manual does not uniquely resolve these cases: all 8 Adult models in Combat when another must appear; whether a destroyed Nest is restored when Queen development adds an Egg; Contamination on successful Egg Melee; and whether later deaths re-unlock Pods after the first death’s unlock was reversed. The critical-moment rule says **first** death, while the Escape Pods section says **any** death. These cases need an original-game publisher clarification or matching official erratum; no ruling is invented here. Specific Action, Item and Weakness effects not reproduced in the manual must be read on their cards.
+The original English manual and supplemental sources do not fully resolve these cases: all 8 Adult models in Combat when another must appear; whether a destroyed Nest is restored when Queen development adds an Egg; how to execute the missed Egg Melee Contamination waiver alongside the normal pre-roll draw; and whether later deaths re-unlock Pods after the first death’s unlock was reversed. The critical-moment rule says **first** death, while the English Escape Pods section says **any** death. The original French/German Pod sections say first death consistently, but are not identified as errata overriding the inconsistent English text. These remaining cases need an original-game publisher clarification or matching official erratum; no ruling is invented here.
+
+The successful Egg Melee ruling above follows the ordinary Melee procedure, corroborated by the explicitly miss-conditioned exception in the publisher-hosted original [Polish manual, p.25](https://awakenrealms.com/images/download/Nemesis/PL/NEMESIS_RULEBOOK_280x280mm_PL.pdf#page=25) and [French manual, p.25](https://awakenrealms.com/images/download/Nemesis/FR/NEMESIS_RULEBOOK_280x280mm_FR.pdf#page=25). The miss procedure remains unresolved; a blanket exemption for all Egg Melee is not established. Specific Action, Item and Weakness effects not reproduced in the manual must be read on their cards.
 
